/* Generated by tools/build.js from data/sc-500.js. Edit that file, not this one. */
CertHub.addQuestions("sc-500", [["az1",0,1,"An engineer needs to give a helpdesk team the ability to reset passwords for non-admin users in Microsoft Entra ID, and nothing else. Which role should be assigned?",["User Administrator","Helpdesk Administrator","Global Reader","Privileged Authentication Administrator"],1,"Helpdesk Administrator can reset passwords for non-administrators and some limited admin roles. User Administrator also manages users and groups, which is more than required.","1: Entra roles"],["az2",0,1,"Admins hold standing Owner rights on production subscriptions. The security team wants them to request Owner only when needed, with MFA and a written reason, for at most four hours. What should be configured?",["An Azure Policy Deny assignment on the Owner role","A Conditional Access policy for the Azure portal app","A custom role with fewer actions than Owner","A PIM eligible assignment with activation settings"],3,"PIM for Azure resources turns Owner into an eligible role that must be activated with MFA and justification for a limited duration. Conditional Access controls sign-in, not standing role membership.","1: Privileged Identity Management"],["az3",0,1,"Which statement about Azure RBAC role assignment inheritance is correct?",["Assignments at a management group are inherited by child subscriptions","Assignments at a resource group apply to the subscription above it","Resource-level assignments override deny assignments","Only Owner assignments are inherited downward"],0,"Azure RBAC assignments flow down the scope hierarchy: management group, subscription, resource group, resource. They never flow upward, and deny assignments take precedence over role assignments.","1: Azure RBAC"],["az4",0,1,"A web app running in App Service must read secrets from Key Vault without any credential stored in code or configuration. What should be used?",["A client secret saved in app settings","The Key Vault access key","A managed identity for the web app","A shared access signature"],2,"A managed identity gets tokens from Microsoft Entra automatically, and the vault grants that identity a role such as Key Vault Secrets User. A client secret in app settings is still a stored credential. Key Vault has no access key or SAS.","1: Managed identities"],["az5",0,1,"Five function apps need identical permissions to a storage account, and the identity must survive the apps being redeployed. Which identity type fits best?",["A system-assigned managed identity on each app","An app registration with a certificate credential","A user-assigned managed identity shared by the apps","A guest account invited into the tenant"],2,"A user-assigned managed identity is a standalone resource that can be attached to many apps and is not deleted with them. System-assigned identities are one per resource and deleted with it.","1: Managed identities"],["az6",0,1,"Users are consenting to third-party apps that request access to their mailbox. The security team wants user consent limited to verified publishers and low-impact permissions, with an admin reviewing other requests. What should they configure?",["User consent settings plus the admin consent workflow","Redirect URI restrictions on each app registration","A Conditional Access policy blocking unknown locations","A PIM access review of the Global Administrators"],0,"User consent settings can restrict consent to verified publishers and selected permissions, and the admin consent workflow routes other requests to reviewers. Redirect URIs do not control consent.","1: App registrations and consent"],["az7",0,1,"What is created in a tenant when a multitenant application is first consented to there?",["A new app registration in the tenant","A user-assigned managed identity for the app","A guest user account for the publisher","A service principal (enterprise application)"],3,"Consent creates a service principal, shown as an enterprise application, representing the app in that tenant. The app registration exists only in the home tenant.","1: App registrations and consent"],["az8",0,1,"A company wants to require MFA for all users signing in to the Azure portal, except when they are on the corporate network. What should be built?",["Per-user MFA enabled for every account in the tenant, with app passwords","A Conditional Access policy for Azure management that excludes a trusted named location","Security defaults with the corporate IP ranges added as trusted IPs","An Azure Policy assignment that audits sign-ins from outside the office"],1,"Conditional Access can target the Azure management app and exclude a named location marked trusted. Security defaults cannot be customized with exclusions, and Azure Policy does not govern sign-in.","1: Conditional Access"],["az9",0,1,"Before enforcing a new Conditional Access policy that blocks legacy authentication, an engineer wants to see which sign-ins it would affect without blocking anyone. What should they do?",["Assign it to an empty group","Set the policy to Report-only","Enable it and review the audit log","Create a PIM access review"],1,"Report-only mode evaluates the policy on every sign-in and logs the result without enforcing it. Enabling it would block users immediately, and an empty group shows no impact at all.","1: Conditional Access"],["az10",0,1,"Administrators must use phishing-resistant sign-in. Which Conditional Access grant control enforces this most directly?",["Require the device to be marked compliant in Intune","Require an approved client app on mobile platforms","Require a password change on every sign-in","Require an authentication strength of phishing-resistant MFA"],3,"Authentication strengths let a policy require specific methods, such as FIDO2 security keys or Windows Hello for Business. A compliant device does not stop an attacker from phishing the credentials themselves.","1: Authentication methods"],["az11",0,1,"A Key Vault uses the access policy model. A user with Contributor on the vault has no access policy but can still read secrets after a few minutes. Why?",["Contributor can edit the vault's access policies and grant itself access","The Contributor role includes secret data actions by default","Soft delete exposes recently deleted secrets to all Contributors","Access policies are ignored for users who hold the Contributor role"],0,"Under access policies, anyone who can write the vault resource can edit its access policies. The RBAC permission model separates management from data access, so Contributor alone cannot read secrets.","1: Key Vault"],["az12",0,1,"An auditor requires that deleted keys in a Key Vault cannot be permanently removed by anyone before the retention period ends. What must be enabled?",["Soft delete only","A ReadOnly resource lock","Purge protection","Key rotation policy"],2,"Purge protection prevents permanent deletion of a vault or its objects while they are in the soft-deleted state, even by administrators. Soft delete alone still allows a purge.","1: Key Vault"],["az13",0,1,"A security engineer wants Azure to rotate a customer-managed key in Key Vault every 90 days automatically. What should be configured?",["A Logic App that deletes the old key","Purge protection on the vault","A key rotation policy on the key","An expiration date on the vault"],2,"Key Vault key rotation policies generate a new key version on a schedule and can notify before expiry. Services that use versionless key URIs pick up the new version automatically.","1: Key Vault"],["az14",0,1,"New storage accounts must never allow public blob access. Existing accounts should be reported but not changed. Which Azure Policy effect meets the requirement for new resources?",["Deny","Audit","AuditIfNotExists","Disabled"],0,"Deny blocks create or update requests that violate the rule, while existing resources are only evaluated and marked non-compliant. Audit would allow new non-compliant accounts.","1: Azure Policy"],["az15",0,1,"A policy must automatically add a diagnostic setting to every new Key Vault that is missing one. Which effect and prerequisite are needed?",["Modify, with no identity required on the assignment","Deny, with a CanNotDelete lock on each vault","Append, with a policy exemption for existing vaults","DeployIfNotExists, with a managed identity for remediation"],3,"DeployIfNotExists deploys a related resource when it is missing, and the assignment needs a managed identity with rights to deploy it. Modify changes properties of the resource itself, such as tags.","1: Azure Policy"],["az16",0,1,"Twenty related policy definitions must be assigned together to many subscriptions and tracked as one compliance score. What should be created?",["A resource lock","A policy initiative","A management group per definition","A custom RBAC role"],1,"An initiative (policy set) groups definitions so they can be assigned and reported together. Management groups are scopes, not groupings of policies.","1: Azure Policy"],["az17",0,1,"An Owner tries to delete a resource group and receives an error even though they have full permissions. What is the most likely cause?",["The Owner role lacks delete actions","The resource group has a CanNotDelete lock","A Conditional Access policy blocks deletions","PIM is enabled for the subscription"],1,"Locks apply to everyone, including Owners, until removed. Owner includes all actions, and Conditional Access evaluates sign-ins, not specific delete operations.","1: Governance"],["az18",0,1,"A ReadOnly lock is placed on a storage account. What unexpected side effect is common?",["Blob data is re-encrypted with a new Microsoft-managed key","Users can no longer sign in to the Azure portal at all","Blob reads through Entra RBAC are blocked on the data plane","Listing the account keys fails because it is a POST operation"],3,"ReadOnly blocks all write and POST management operations, and listing keys is a POST, so tools that fetch keys break. Data-plane access through Entra RBAC is not blocked by the lock.","1: Governance"],["az19",0,1,"A team needs a role that can restart VMs and read their configuration but cannot create or delete them. No built-in role matches. What should be created?",["A custom Azure role with the needed actions","A Microsoft Entra administrative unit","A PIM approval workflow","An Azure Policy initiative"],0,"A custom role lists exactly the allowed actions, such as Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/read and restart/action, with assignable scopes. Administrative units scope Entra directory roles, not Azure resource actions.","1: Azure RBAC"],["az20",0,1,"Which field in a custom Azure role definition grants permission to read blob contents rather than manage the storage account?",["actions","notActions","dataActions","assignableScopes"],2,"dataActions cover data-plane operations such as reading blobs or queue messages. actions cover control-plane operations on the resource itself.","1: Azure RBAC"],["az21",0,1,"The CISO wants guest users with access to production resource groups reviewed by resource owners every quarter, with access removed if not approved. What should be used?",["Azure Policy compliance reports","Defender for Cloud secure score","Microsoft Entra access reviews","Resource locks on each group"],2,"Access reviews run recurring reviews of group memberships, app assignments or role assignments and can auto-remove denied access. Policy compliance does not review who has access.","1: Governance"],["az22",0,1,"Microsoft Entra ID Protection reports a user as high risk after leaked credentials were found. Which control forces a secure password change at next sign-in?",["A user risk Conditional Access policy requiring password change","A sign-in frequency session control set to one hour","A named location that marks the office network as trusted","A Key Vault access policy that removes the user's secrets"],0,"User risk reflects the likelihood an identity is compromised, and a risk-based policy can require a secure password change with MFA. Sign-in frequency only changes how often users reauthenticate.","1: Identity protection"],["az23",0,2,"A developer needs to give a partner time-limited read access to one blob container. The storage account has key access disabled. Which SAS type can still be used?",["Account SAS","Service SAS","Stored access policy SAS","User delegation SAS"],3,"A user delegation SAS is signed with a key obtained through Entra credentials, so it works when Shared Key is disabled. Account and service SAS are signed with the account key.","2: Storage"],["az24",0,2,"A service SAS was issued with a one-year expiry and must be revoked today without affecting other SAS tokens signed with the same key. What should have been done when it was issued?",["Sign it with the secondary account key","Link it to a stored access policy","Set the HTTPS-only protocol flag on it","Include a narrow allowed IP address range"],1,"A SAS tied to a stored access policy can be revoked by changing or deleting that policy. Rotating the signing key would invalidate every SAS signed with it.","2: Storage"],["az25",0,2,"Compliance requires that financial records in Blob Storage cannot be modified or deleted for seven years, even by account owners. What should be configured?",["Soft delete for blobs with a 7-year retention","A locked time-based immutability (WORM) policy","A CanNotDelete resource lock on the account","Customer-managed keys with a rotation policy"],1,"A locked time-based retention policy makes blobs write-once, read-many for the retention period. A resource lock blocks deleting the account, not changing blob data.","2: Storage"],["az26",0,2,"A regulator requires that the company control and be able to revoke the keys that encrypt a storage account. What should be enabled?",["Infrastructure encryption with Microsoft-managed keys","HTTPS-only secure transfer","A user delegation SAS","Customer-managed keys stored in Key Vault"],3,"Customer-managed keys let the organization own, rotate and revoke the key in Key Vault or Managed HSM. Infrastructure encryption adds a second layer but with Microsoft-managed keys.","2: Storage"],["az27",0,2,"Uploaded files in a storage account should be checked for malware as they arrive, and the result written as a blob index tag. Which feature fits?",["Defender for Storage malware scanning","An Azure Policy DeployIfNotExists assignment","Blob soft delete with versioning turned on","Network Watcher packet capture on the subnet"],0,"Defender for Storage on-upload malware scanning scans new blobs and can tag results and raise alerts. The other options do not inspect file content.","2: Storage"],["az28",0,2,"A storage account firewall allows only selected VNets. Azure Backup and Azure Monitor now fail to reach it. What is the simplest fix?",["Enable public network access from all networks instead","Rotate both account keys and update the services","Allow trusted Microsoft services to access the account","Disable secure transfer so the services can use HTTP"],2,"The trusted Microsoft services exception lets listed Azure services reach the account despite network rules. Opening all networks removes the protection entirely.","2: Storage"],["az29",0,2,"An Azure SQL logical server must allow only Microsoft Entra identities to sign in, and SQL authentication must be refused. What should be enabled?",["Transparent data encryption","Dynamic data masking","Microsoft Entra-only authentication","Advanced Threat Protection email alerts"],2,"Entra-only authentication disables SQL logins for the server. TDE encrypts data at rest and does not affect sign-in.","2: Databases"],["az30",0,2,"A payroll app stores national ID numbers in Azure SQL. DBAs must not be able to see plaintext values, even with sysadmin rights. What should be used?",["Always Encrypted","Dynamic data masking","Transparent data encryption","Row-level security"],0,"Always Encrypted encrypts columns on the client; keys never reach the database engine, so DBAs see only ciphertext. Dynamic data masking can be bypassed by privileged users and TDE decrypts data for any authorized query.","2: Databases"],["az31",0,2,"Support staff should see only the last four digits of customer phone numbers in query results, while the app sees full values. No application changes are allowed. What fits?",["Always Encrypted","TDE with customer-managed keys","Server-level firewall rules","Dynamic data masking"],3,"Dynamic data masking hides data in result sets for users without UNMASK permission, with no app changes. Always Encrypted requires driver changes and hides the whole value.","2: Databases"],["az32",0,2,"The security team wants to be alerted to SQL injection attempts and anomalous logins against Azure SQL databases. What should be enabled?",["SQL auditing to a storage account only","Microsoft Defender for SQL","Always Encrypted","Geo-replication"],1,"Defender for SQL provides vulnerability assessment and threat detection, including SQL injection and unusual access alerts. Auditing records events but does not analyze them for threats.","2: Databases"],["az33",0,2,"An NSG has rule 200 denying TCP 3389 from Internet and rule 100 allowing TCP 3389 from 203.0.113.10. What happens to RDP from 203.0.113.10?",["It is denied, because deny rules always take precedence","It is allowed, because rule 100 is processed first","It is denied by the DenyAllInBound default rule","It depends on the route table attached to the subnet"],1,"NSG rules are processed in priority order from lowest number, and the first match decides. Deny rules do not automatically override allows.","2: Networking"],["az34",0,2,"Web and database VMs share one subnet. The team wants NSG rules that say 'web servers may reach database servers on 1433' without listing IP addresses. What should be used?",["Service tags","User-defined routes","Private DNS zone records","Application security groups"],3,"Application security groups group VM NICs by role so NSG rules can reference them instead of IPs. Service tags represent Azure service address ranges, not your VMs.","2: Networking"],["az35",0,2,"An NSG outbound rule should allow VMs to reach Azure Storage in their region only, without tracking Microsoft's IP ranges. What should the destination be?",["The regional Storage service tag","An application security group for storage","The VirtualNetwork service tag","A static list of Azure public IP prefixes"],0,"Regional service tags such as Storage.WestEurope are maintained by Microsoft and update automatically. The VirtualNetwork tag covers your address spaces, not Azure services.","2: Networking"],["az36",0,2,"The central network team must block inbound SSH from the internet across 200 VNets, and application teams must not be able to override it with their own NSGs. What should be used?",["An NSG on every subnet that app teams manage themselves","Service endpoints enabled on every subnet in each VNet","Azure Virtual Network Manager security admin rules","Azure DDoS Network Protection on each virtual network"],2,"Security admin rules in Virtual Network Manager are evaluated before NSGs and can deny traffic that NSGs cannot re-allow. NSGs owned by app teams could be changed by those teams.","2: Networking"],["az37",0,2,"An Azure SQL database must be reachable only through a private IP from the VNet and from on-premises over ExpressRoute, with public access disabled. What should be implemented?",["A service endpoint for Microsoft.Sql on the subnet","A server firewall rule for the VNet address range","A private endpoint with a private DNS zone","An application security group for the database tier"],2,"A private endpoint gives the database a private IP reachable from the VNet, peered VNets and on-premises. Service endpoints only work from the enabled subnet and keep the public endpoint.","2: Networking"],["az38",0,2,"After creating a private endpoint for a storage account, VMs still resolve the account's name to its public IP. What is most likely missing?",["A privatelink private DNS zone linked to the VNet","An NSG rule allowing outbound port 443 to Storage","Customer-managed keys configured on the account","A user-defined route sending 0.0.0.0/0 to the internet"],0,"Name resolution must return the private IP, which is done by the privatelink private DNS zone linked to the VNet (or equivalent custom DNS). NSG rules do not change DNS answers.","2: Networking"],["az39",0,2,"Outbound HTTPS traffic from workloads must be decrypted and checked against intrusion signatures. Which service meets this?",["Azure Firewall Standard","NSG flow logs","Application Gateway Basic","Azure Firewall Premium"],3,"Azure Firewall Premium adds TLS inspection and signature-based IDPS. Standard offers threat intelligence filtering but does not decrypt TLS.","2: Networking"],["az40",0,2,"All internet-bound traffic from a spoke subnet must pass through an Azure Firewall in the hub. What must be configured on the spoke subnet?",["An NSG on the spoke subnet that denies all outbound internet traffic","A route table with 0.0.0.0/0 pointing to the firewall's private IP","A service endpoint for Microsoft.Web on the spoke subnet","A private DNS zone for the firewall linked to the spoke VNet"],1,"A user-defined route for 0.0.0.0/0 with the firewall's private IP as the virtual appliance next hop forces traffic through it. An NSG deny would block the traffic instead of redirecting it.","2: Networking"],["az41",0,2,"A public web app behind Application Gateway suffers SQL injection and cross-site scripting attempts. What should be enabled on the gateway?",["DDoS Network Protection on the gateway's VNet","Web Application Firewall with a managed rule set","NSG flow logs on the gateway subnet","A private endpoint for the backend app"],1,"WAF on Application Gateway inspects HTTP requests using managed OWASP-based rules to block injection and XSS. DDoS Protection handles volumetric attacks, not application-layer payloads.","2: Networking"],["az42",0,2,"A company wants to publish a global web app with edge caching and layer 7 protection close to users worldwide. Which combination fits?",["Application Gateway with a public IP in one region","Azure Firewall Standard in each spoke","VPN Gateway with forced tunneling","Azure Front Door with a WAF policy"],3,"Front Door is a global edge service and its WAF policy filters traffic at the edge. Application Gateway is regional.","2: Networking"],["az43",0,2,"Remote workers need access to specific private apps in Azure without a full network-level VPN, based on identity and Conditional Access. What fits?",["Microsoft Entra Private Access","Point-to-site VPN with certificate auth","A site-to-site VPN","Azure Bastion"],0,"Entra Private Access is a zero trust network access service that publishes private apps per identity with Conditional Access. A point-to-site VPN gives network-level access to the VNet.","2: Networking"],["az44",0,2,"A VM cannot reach a database on port 1433. The engineer wants to know which NSG rule is dropping the packet. Which tool answers this fastest?",["Azure Advisor","Defender for Cloud secure score","Network Watcher IP flow verify","Azure Monitor autoscale"],2,"IP flow verify tests a specific 5-tuple against the effective NSG rules and names the rule that allows or denies it. Advisor gives general recommendations.","2: Networking"],["az45",0,2,"The security team wants a record of accepted and denied traffic across a VNet, with visual analysis of top talkers. What should be enabled?",["Boot diagnostics on every virtual machine","Connection troubleshoot on each VM","VNet flow logs with traffic analytics","Azure Monitor metrics alerts on each NIC"],2,"VNet flow logs record allowed and denied flows to storage and traffic analytics processes them in Log Analytics. Connection troubleshoot tests one connection at a time.","2: Networking"],["az46",0,2,"A company has 30 branch offices and several Azure regions and wants centrally managed connectivity with Azure Firewall inspection in each hub. What fits best?",["Virtual WAN with secured virtual hubs","One hub VNet peered directly to every branch office","A point-to-site VPN client for each branch user","Service endpoints on every subnet in every region"],0,"Virtual WAN provides managed hubs for branch VPN, ExpressRoute and user VPN, and a secured hub adds Azure Firewall managed through Firewall Manager. Branches cannot be peered as VNets.","2: Networking"],["az47",0,2,"Public IP addresses in front of critical workloads need adaptive tuning, attack telemetry and cost protection against volumetric attacks. What should be enabled?",["Azure Firewall Basic SKU","Front Door WAF custom rules","NSG default inbound deny rules","Azure DDoS Protection"],3,"Azure DDoS Protection adds adaptive tuning, attack metrics and alerts, and cost protection beyond the default infrastructure protection. WAF addresses application-layer attacks.","2: Networking"],["az48",0,3,"Management ports on VMs must be closed by default and opened only for a requested source IP for a few hours. What should be enabled?",["Azure Bastion Developer","Just-in-time VM access","An NSG allowing 3389 from any","Encryption at host"],1,"JIT, part of Defender for Servers Plan 2, keeps ports closed and adds temporary allow rules on approved requests. Bastion removes the need for public ports but does not open them on request.","3: Servers and VMs"],["az49",0,3,"Admins need RDP and SSH to VMs from the Azure portal without assigning public IPs to the VMs. What should be deployed?",["A NAT gateway","Azure Bastion","Application Gateway","A public load balancer"],1,"Bastion brokers RDP/SSH over TLS from the portal to the VM's private IP. A NAT gateway only handles outbound traffic.","3: Servers and VMs"],["az50",0,3,"A new Windows VM must be protected against bootkits and rootkits with measured boot and a virtual TPM. Which option should be selected at creation?",["Azure Disk Encryption with BitLocker keys","Encryption at host with platform-managed keys","A dedicated host isolated for the company","Trusted launch (secure boot and vTPM)"],3,"Trusted launch provides secure boot, vTPM and boot integrity monitoring. Disk encryption protects data at rest, not the boot chain.","3: Servers and VMs"],["az51",0,3,"VM temporary disks and disk caches must be encrypted, and no agent may run inside the guest OS. What should be enabled?",["Encryption at host","Azure Disk Encryption","Always Encrypted","Storage Service Encryption only"],0,"Encryption at host encrypts temp disks and caches at the host level without an in-guest agent. Azure Disk Encryption uses BitLocker or DM-Crypt inside the guest.","3: Servers and VMs"],["az52",0,3,"On-premises and AWS servers should appear in Defender for Cloud and receive Defender for Servers protection alongside Azure VMs. What should be deployed on those servers?",["An Azure Bastion host in a peered VNet","A site-to-site VPN Gateway to each location","The Azure Connected Machine agent (Azure Arc)","The legacy Log Analytics (MMA) agent"],2,"Azure Arc projects servers outside Azure as Azure resources so Defender for Servers and Azure Policy can apply. The legacy Log Analytics agent is retired. AWS servers can also be onboarded through the AWS connector, which uses Arc.","3: Servers and VMs"],["az53",0,3,"Which Defender for Servers plan includes just-in-time VM access and file integrity monitoring?",["Plan 1","Foundational CSPM","Plan 2","Defender for Storage"],2,"Plan 2 includes JIT, file integrity monitoring, agentless scanning and more. Plan 1 focuses on Defender for Endpoint integration.","3: Servers and VMs"],["az54",0,3,"The team wants to find missing OS updates on Azure and Arc-enabled servers and schedule patching windows. Which service fits?",["Azure Update Manager","Azure Advisor recommendations","Network Watcher connection monitor","Microsoft Purview Audit"],0,"Azure Update Manager assesses and installs updates on Azure and Arc-enabled machines with maintenance schedules. Advisor does not deploy patches.","3: Servers and VMs"],["az55",0,3,"Developers use kubectl with a shared admin kubeconfig for an AKS cluster. Security wants per-user sign-in with Entra ID and access governed by Azure roles. What should be enabled?",["Kubernetes network policies on each namespace","A private cluster with no public API endpoint","Defender for Containers runtime protection","Entra ID integration with Azure RBAC for Kubernetes"],3,"Entra integration authenticates users with Entra ID, and Azure RBAC for Kubernetes authorizes them through Azure role assignments; local accounts can then be disabled. Network policies control pod traffic, not user access.","3: App platforms"],["az56",0,3,"The AKS API server must not be reachable from the internet at all. What should be configured?",["Authorized IP ranges only","A private cluster","A Kubernetes network policy","An Azure Policy add-on"],1,"A private cluster gives the API server a private IP only reachable from the VNet. Authorized IP ranges still expose a public endpoint, just filtered.","3: App platforms"],["az57",0,3,"Pods in the 'frontend' namespace must be allowed to reach 'backend' pods, and all other pod-to-pod traffic to backend must be blocked. What should be used?",["An NSG on the node pool subnet","Kubernetes network policies","Azure Firewall DNAT rules for the pods","Azure Bastion connected to the cluster"],1,"Network policies (Azure, Calico or Cilium) filter traffic between pods using labels and namespaces. NSGs work on node or subnet IPs and cannot see pod labels.","3: App platforms"],["az58",0,3,"A security team wants vulnerability assessment of container images, runtime threat detection on AKS nodes, and Kubernetes posture recommendations. Which plan provides this?",["Defender for App Service","Defender for Key Vault","Defender for Storage","Defender for Containers"],3,"Defender for Containers covers image vulnerability assessment, run-time protection and Kubernetes hardening for AKS and other clusters. The other plans cover different resource types.","3: App platforms"],["az59",0,3,"AKS pulls images from Azure Container Registry using the registry's admin user password stored as a Kubernetes secret. What is the recommended replacement?",["Give the kubelet identity AcrPull and disable the admin user","Keep the admin user but rotate its password every month","Store the admin password in a ConfigMap instead of a secret","Make the registry public so no credentials are needed"],0,"Attaching ACR with the kubelet managed identity and AcrPull gives least-privilege, secretless pulls. Rotating a shared admin password keeps a shared credential with push rights.","3: App platforms"],["az60",0,3,"An App Service app stores a database connection string in plain text in app settings. The team wants it kept in Key Vault without code changes. What should they use?",["A deployment slot setting marked sticky to production","An Azure Policy Modify effect that encrypts app settings","A Key Vault reference using the app's managed identity","Easy Auth with Microsoft Entra ID for the web app"],2,"A Key Vault reference (@Microsoft.KeyVault(...)) resolves the secret at runtime using the app's managed identity, with no code change. Slot settings only control swap behavior.","3: App platforms"],["az61",0,3,"An internal App Service app should accept traffic only from the company's Application Gateway subnet. What should be configured?",["HTTPS only enabled on the web app","A minimum inbound TLS version of 1.2","Access restrictions allowing that subnet","A custom domain with a managed certificate"],2,"Access restrictions filter inbound requests by IP, service tag or VNet subnet. HTTPS only and TLS version protect traffic in transit but do not restrict sources.","3: App platforms"],["az62",0,3,"A company wants users to sign in to an App Service web app with Microsoft Entra ID without writing authentication code. What should be enabled?",["App Service built-in authentication (Easy Auth)","A private endpoint for the web app's inbound traffic","Access restrictions that allow only the corporate IPs","A system-assigned managed identity on the web app"],0,"Built-in authentication handles sign-in with Entra ID and other providers before requests reach the code. A managed identity lets the app call other services, not users sign in.","3: App platforms"],["az63",0,3,"An HTTP-triggered Azure Function uses a function key that has been shared widely. Which change best reduces risk while keeping callers working after an update?",["Change the authorization level to anonymous","Move the function key into the URL query string","Enable remote debugging to trace the callers","Require Entra ID authentication and use tokens"],3,"Using Entra authentication gives identity-based, revocable access instead of a shared key. Anonymous removes protection entirely.","3: App platforms"],["az64",0,3,"A Logic App must call an Azure Resource Manager API. The team wants no stored credentials in the workflow. What should they use?",["A client secret in a parameter","A managed identity on the Logic App","A storage account key","A SAS token in the trigger URL"],1,"Logic Apps can authenticate outbound calls with a managed identity that holds the needed Azure role. A client secret is still a stored credential.","3: App platforms"],["az65",0,3,"A generative AI chatbot built on Microsoft Foundry is being hit with prompts that try to override its system instructions. The security team wants alerts in Defender for Cloud. What should be enabled?",["Defender for Storage on the training data","Defender for AI services threat protection","Just-in-time VM access for the app servers","Azure DDoS Protection on the public endpoint"],1,"Defender for AI services raises alerts for threats such as jailbreak and prompt injection attempts against AI workloads, using Prompt Shields signals. DDoS Protection handles network floods.","3: Security for AI"],["az66",0,3,"Several apps call the same Azure OpenAI deployment with API keys, and one app consumes most of the tokens. The team wants central authentication and per-app token limits. What should be deployed?",["A private endpoint for each calling app","A separate Azure OpenAI resource per app","An NSG in front of the OpenAI resource","An AI Gateway in API Management"],3,"An API Management AI gateway can authenticate to the backend with a managed identity and apply token limit policies per consumer. Private endpoints restrict network paths but do not enforce quotas.","3: Security for AI"],["az67",0,3,"Before rolling out Microsoft 365 Copilot, the company wants to find sensitive files that are overshared and could surface in Copilot answers. Which tool fits?",["Microsoft Purview DSPM for AI","Azure Firewall Premium TLS inspection","Defender for Servers file integrity monitoring","Network Watcher traffic analytics"],0,"Purview Data Security Posture Management for AI reports oversharing and sensitive data exposure risks for Copilot and other AI apps. The other tools do not analyze data exposure in Microsoft 365.","3: Security for AI"],["az68",0,3,"AI agents in the tenant act with their own identities. The security team wants to block agents from signing in when they are flagged as risky. Which feature supports this?",["A resource lock on the agent","An NSG on the agent subnet","Conditional Access for Microsoft Entra Agent ID","Azure Policy Audit effect"],2,"Microsoft Entra Agent ID gives agents identities that Conditional Access policies can target, including risk-based blocking. Resource locks and NSGs do not control identity sign-in.","3: Security for AI"],["az69",0,3,"A Foundry model should reject inputs that contain hate speech and should flag outputs that include protected material. What should be configured?",["A WAF custom rule on the Front Door profile","Key Vault purge protection on the model's vault","Content filters and guardrails on the deployment","Transparent data encryption on the chat history"],2,"Foundry deployments use content filters and guardrails (Azure AI Content Safety) to screen prompts and completions. A WAF inspects HTTP patterns, not model content categories.","3: Security for AI"],["az70",0,4,"The security team wants to see chains such as 'internet-exposed VM with a critical vulnerability and a managed identity that can read sensitive storage'. Which Defender for Cloud feature shows this?",["Attack path analysis in Defender CSPM","The regulatory compliance dashboard view","Workflow automation with a Logic App","Secure score history in the overview blade"],0,"Attack path analysis, part of the paid Defender CSPM plan, maps exploitable paths to high-value assets. The compliance dashboard only maps controls to standards.","4: Defender for Cloud"],["az71",0,4,"Which capability is included in free foundational CSPM?",["Attack path analysis","Agentless vulnerability scanning","Cloud security explorer queries","Secure score and security recommendations"],3,"Foundational CSPM includes secure score, recommendations, asset inventory and the Microsoft cloud security benchmark. The others require Defender CSPM.","4: Defender for Cloud"],["az72",0,4,"An engineer fixes a recommendation on 8 of 10 storage accounts. How does secure score change for that control?",["It gains the full control score immediately","It gains points in proportion to the healthy resources","It does not change until the next monthly recalculation","It drops, because partial remediation is penalized"],1,"Secure score awards control points in proportion to healthy resources, and the full points only when every resource is healthy. Scores refresh within hours, not monthly.","4: Defender for Cloud"],["az73",0,4,"An auditor wants to see how the Azure environment maps to PCI DSS controls. Where should the engineer add this?",["Import a PCI template from the Sentinel workbooks gallery","Add the standard in regulatory compliance","Filter the Azure Advisor recommendations by PCI tag","Run an Entra ID access review scoped to cardholder apps"],1,"The regulatory compliance dashboard assesses resources against the Microsoft cloud security benchmark and extra standards such as PCI DSS that you add. Workbooks visualize data but do not assess compliance.","4: Defender for Cloud"],["az74",0,4,"Recommendations keep being ignored. The CISO wants each one assigned to a resource owner with a due date and email reminders. What should be configured?",["A Sentinel watchlist","An Azure Policy exemption","A resource lock","Governance rules in Defender for Cloud"],3,"Governance rules assign owners and due dates to recommendations automatically and send reminders. An exemption would hide the recommendation instead of fixing it.","4: Defender for Cloud"],["az75",0,4,"The company also runs workloads in AWS and wants their posture in the same Defender for Cloud secure score. What should be created?",["An AWS connector in Defender for Cloud","A site-to-site VPN between Azure and AWS","A Sentinel watchlist that lists the AWS account IDs","A management group named AWS with the accounts in it"],0,"Multicloud connectors onboard AWS accounts and GCP projects for posture management and workload protection. A VPN only provides network connectivity.","4: Defender for Cloud"],["az76",0,4,"Every high-severity Defender for Cloud alert should automatically trigger a Logic App that opens a ticket. What should be configured?",["A Sentinel hunting query","An Azure Policy Audit effect","Workflow automation in Defender for Cloud","A Key Vault rotation policy"],2,"Workflow automation runs a Logic App when alerts, recommendations or compliance changes match your conditions. Hunting queries are run manually.","4: Defender for Cloud"],["az77",0,4,"A Linux appliance sends CEF-formatted logs. How should they be collected into Microsoft Sentinel today?",["The legacy Log Analytics agent installed directly on the appliance","A daily script that uploads the log files to a storage account","A Linux forwarder running the Azure Monitor Agent with a CEF via AMA rule","The appliance configured to send syslog to the Sentinel portal URL"],2,"The supported method uses the Azure Monitor Agent on a forwarder and a data collection rule through the CEF via AMA connector. The legacy Log Analytics agent is retired.","4: Sentinel"],["az78",0,4,"An analyst wants a Sentinel rule that detects role assignment creation within about a minute of it happening. Which rule type is designed for this?",["Near-real-time (NRT) analytics rule","Scheduled rule running every 24 hours","Anomaly rule","Hunting bookmark"],0,"NRT rules run every minute over the latest data for fast detection. A daily scheduled rule would be too slow, and bookmarks are not detections.","4: Sentinel"],["az79",0,4,"Sentinel incidents from a noisy test subscription should automatically be closed as benign, and all others assigned to the tier 1 queue. What should be used?",["A playbook for each incident","A workbook","A watchlist","Automation rules"],3,"Automation rules handle simple triage such as changing status, assigning owners and adding tags without a Logic App. Playbooks are for external or multi-step actions.","4: Sentinel"],["az80",0,4,"When a Sentinel incident involves a compromised user, the SOC wants to disable the account in Entra ID and post in a Teams channel automatically. What should be built?",["An analytics rule with entity mapping enabled","A playbook triggered by an automation rule","A saved hunting query with a livestream","A data collection rule with a transformation"],1,"Playbooks carry out external actions such as disabling users or posting messages, and an automation rule can trigger them on incident creation. Entity mapping only identifies entities.","4: Sentinel"],["az81",0,4,"Analytics rule results should show the affected user and host so incidents can be correlated and investigated in the graph. What should be configured in the rule?",["Alert grouping disabled","Entity mapping","A shorter lookback","Suppression"],1,"Entity mapping tells Sentinel which query columns are accounts, hosts, IPs and so on, enabling correlation and investigation. Suppression stops the rule from running after a match.","4: Sentinel"],["az82",0,4,"The SOC maintains a list of VIP accounts that analytics rules should treat as high priority. Where should the list live so KQL can reference it?",["A Key Vault secret","An Azure Policy parameter","A resource tag","A Sentinel watchlist"],3,"Watchlists are uploaded lists that KQL can join with the _GetWatchlist() function. Key Vault and policy parameters are not queryable from Sentinel rules.","4: Sentinel"],["az83",0,4,"Firewall logs must be kept for two years for investigations, but are rarely queried and are too costly in the Analytics tier. What should the engineer consider?",["A lower-cost long-term tier such as the Sentinel data lake","Deleting the logs after 30 days to stay within budget","Copying each day's logs into a Sentinel watchlist","Disabling the firewall connector until an incident occurs"],0,"Lower-cost tiers keep high-volume, rarely queried data for long periods at reduced cost while still allowing queries. Deleting logs breaks the retention requirement.","4: Sentinel"],["az84",0,4,"A threat hunter wants to look proactively for signs of an attacker technique that has no alert yet, and save interesting results for later. What should be used?",["Workflow automation in Defender for Cloud","Automation rules that close incidents","Hunting queries and bookmarks","Secure score recommendations"],2,"Hunting queries search data for indicators, and bookmarks save results for investigation or promotion to incidents. Automation rules act on incidents that already exist.","4: Sentinel"],["az85",0,4,"Which KQL query returns failed sign-ins from the last hour grouped by user?",["SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(1h) and ResultType == \"0\" | summarize count() by UserPrincipalName","AuditLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(1h) | summarize count() by OperationName, Identity","SigninLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(1h) and ResultType != \"0\" | summarize count() by UserPrincipalName","SecurityEvent | where TimeGenerated > ago(1h) and EventID == 4624 | summarize count() by Account"],2,"ResultType 0 means success, so != \"0\" returns failures, and summarize groups by user. The other queries return successful sign-ins or unrelated data.","4: Sentinel"],["az86",0,4,"Users report that Microsoft Security Copilot responses are slow and prompts are being throttled during a busy incident. What is the most likely fix?",["Provision more SCUs or allow overage","Assign all analysts the Security Reader role","Enable more Sentinel data connectors","Disable promptbooks for the whole tenant"],0,"Security Copilot capacity is measured in SCUs, and throttling means capacity is exhausted. Adding roles or connectors does not add capacity.","4: Security Copilot"],["az87",0,4,"An analyst wants Security Copilot to run the same series of prompts for every phishing investigation. What should they create?",["A watchlist","A workbook","A data collection rule","A promptbook"],3,"Promptbooks are saved sequences of prompts that can be run together with inputs. Workbooks visualize data and do not run Copilot prompts.","4: Security Copilot"],["az88",0,4,"Security Copilot needs to answer questions using data from a third-party threat intelligence service. What should be added?",["A new SCU region","A plugin for that service","A Sentinel automation rule","A Purview sensitivity label"],1,"Plugins extend Security Copilot with data and skills from Microsoft and third-party sources. SCUs add capacity, not new data sources.","4: Security Copilot"],["az89",0,4,"During an investigation, the team needs to know who deleted a SharePoint file and when. Which tool records this activity?",["Defender for Cloud secure score","Microsoft Purview Audit","Network Watcher flow logs","Azure Update Manager"],1,"Purview Audit (unified audit log) records user and admin activity across Microsoft 365, including file deletions. Flow logs only record network traffic.","4: Operations"],["az90",0,4,"A company wants Microsoft Defender XDR incidents, including those from Defender for Cloud, to flow into Sentinel without creating duplicate incidents. What should be used?",["A separate scheduled analytics rule for each Defender alert","A daily CSV export of alerts imported into a custom table","A watchlist of alert IDs joined to the SecurityAlert table","The Defender XDR connector with incident integration"],3,"The Defender XDR connector syncs incidents and alerts bidirectionally, avoiding duplicates. Separate rules per alert would create duplicate incidents.","4: Sentinel"]]);
